{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\, & ={\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/25)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/25}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f58488b23f0bf4c4f5a30495a2c8a6772ea09cb609f9ecdd35e14c31759c9642"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-49546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=8\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $8x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=8x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8\\int \\frac{1}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =8\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f58488b23f0bf4c4f5a30495a2c8a6772ea09cb609f9ecdd35e14c31759c9642"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(4x)}{4}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(8x)}{8}+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(64x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int \\frac{1}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $5x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{5|x|\\sqrt{25{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{|5x|\\sqrt{(5x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f58488b23f0bf4c4f5a30495a2c8a6772ea09cb609f9ecdd35e14c31759c9642"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{arctan}(5x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\text{arctan}(5x)}{5}+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-73718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{arcsec}(5x)}{5}+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $5{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}.$\n\nThus, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{5}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f58488b23f0bf4c4f5a30495a2c8a6772ea09cb609f9ecdd35e14c31759c9642"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-114035" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-346451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-346451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-346451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f58488b23f0bf4c4f5a30495a2c8a6772ea09cb609f9ecdd35e14c31759c9642"} {"question" "q-346451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-346451" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013963/state.json" "file_sha256" "ac452adc6028eeb359f49d07e55076d688fcb29d94bc69728ad2e2348abc3bae"} {"question" "q-69476" "field" "selection" "attrib